WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.840
Who lives? Who dies? Who returns to the afterlife&nbsp;
from whence they came? And most importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.320
who gets slimed? This is the ending of&nbsp;
"Ghostbusters: Afterlife," explained.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.960
Obviously, spoilers ahead.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.960
Arguably the most important character in&nbsp;
Ghostbusters: Afterlife is Phoebe, the brilliant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:21.280
young granddaughter of Egon Spengler. It's Phoebe&nbsp;
who cracks open the mystery at the heart of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.760
film and forms a connection across generations&nbsp;
of her estranged family in the process.&nbsp;

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.040
At the beginning of the film, Phoebe&nbsp;
is an outsider not just in Summerville,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:33.360
but in her own family. By the end of the film,&nbsp;
she's the heart of her extended new family and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.360
friend group, a hero to the world, and&nbsp;
a newly minted Ghostbuster, continuing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:42.080
the tradition set up by her late grandfather.
We see Phoebe's journey to self-actualization,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:47.120
but the question remains: What happens to her&nbsp;
next? It's easy to imagine her as the first junior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.520
member of the Ghostbusters, attending a fancy&nbsp;
science-based New York City school by day and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:56.400
wielding a proton pack by night. It's also easy&nbsp;
to see her staying in Summerville for a while,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.120
archiving and continuing her grandfather's work&nbsp;
as she digs deeper into the mysteries of Gozer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.360
Whatever happens, Phoebe has a bright future not&nbsp;
just because of what she's achieved, but because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:08.000
she's learned how to really be herself.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.760
Though his personal journey in the film is&nbsp;
considerably less developed than his sister's,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.600
Trevor Spengler still gets an arc across&nbsp;
"Ghostbusters: Afterlife." Though he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.680
definitely considers himself the cool one in&nbsp;
his family, Trevor is still a bit of an outsider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.360
thanks to his fresh arrival in Summerville.
By the end of the film, Trevor has become a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:28.000
Ghostbuster of sorts alongside his sister, despite&nbsp;
his lack of scientific knowledge or particular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:33.280
enthusiasm for the paranormal. What he does have,&nbsp;
though, is a sizable sense of mechanical wisdom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:38.160
as evidenced by his ability to fix ECTO-1 with&nbsp;
only a tiny bit of supernatural help from his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.400
grandfather. It's easy to see him sticking&nbsp;
around Summerville, but it's just as easy to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.320
see him moving to New York City, where Trevor&nbsp;
could become the Winston of the next generation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:51.520
of Ghostbusters. He's not a scientist, but he's a&nbsp;
hard worker with a sharp mind, and he's willing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:54.400
dig in deep for the people he cares about.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.520
At the beginning of the film, Callie&nbsp;
Spengler feels like a failed mother.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:01.440
She hasn't been able to make life in the city&nbsp;
work out, her kids are growing and changing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:05.520
in ways she doesn't fully understand, and&nbsp;
her only refuge in life is a broken down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:10.240
old house in the middle of Oklahoma, left to&nbsp;
her by a father who never had time for her.&nbsp;

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:14.560
But like every other member of her family, over&nbsp;
the course of the story Callie finds a new sense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:18.880
of purpose and realizes the father she never&nbsp;
really knew not only cared about her, but did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.200
everything he could to protect her from forces she&nbsp;
couldn't understand at the time. That new sense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:28.000
of purpose also comes through the arrival of Gary&nbsp;
Grooberson, the local seismologist and teacher who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:33.520
not only adores her, but adores her kids as well.
So, what happens to them next? Having made peace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.440
with her family's past, Callie seems ready to&nbsp;
build a new future with Gary, whether that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:42.400
in Summerville, New York City, or somewhere else&nbsp;
entirely. A new family unit has grown out of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.560
ashes of the old one.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.600
Though much of the film centers on&nbsp;
the Spengler family, a good portion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:52.160
of the plot in "Ghostbusters: Afterlife" is&nbsp;
pushed forward by the kid known as Podcast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:56.560
Phoebe's summer school friend with a deep interest&nbsp;
in mysteries and other assorted occult lore.&nbsp;

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.320
Though Phoebe brings the scientific know-how&nbsp;
and observational powers to the team,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:04.400
Podcast brings the belief in the supernatural that&nbsp;
allows her to see what's right in front of her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:08.720
and the research skills to dig into what's really&nbsp;
going on. By the end of the film, it's clear that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:13.040
he's basically the Raymond Stantz of the new&nbsp;
Ghostbusters team, and Ray himself makes it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.440
clear that he's a fan of the young podcaster.
Obviously, Podcast's role in what went down in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.080
Oklahoma could mean a big boost to his subscriber&nbsp;
base, provided enough people know that anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:26.000
went down at all, but it will also mean his&nbsp;
appetite for more supernatural mysteries will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.000
only grow with time.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.640
"Ghostbusters: Afterlife" is largely set in&nbsp;
Summerville, Oklahoma, an out of the way former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.600
mining town that's basically a tiny dot on the map&nbsp;
with seemingly nothing to show for itself. By the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:41.600
end of the film, though, Summerville has become&nbsp;
the epicenter of supernatural activity on Earth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:46.240
as the discovery of a temple built by an eccentric&nbsp;
architect to summon an ancient Sumerian god&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:51.120
propels the Ghostbusters into a new adventure.
After Gozer is trapped by the team, things seem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:55.520
poised to quiet down in Summerville, and we&nbsp;
see the old ECTO-1 car back in action in New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.520 --> 00:04:00.320
York City, but that doesn't mean the Oklahoma&nbsp;
town won't get any more attention. If it truly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:04.560
did serve as the force behind a supernatural&nbsp;
re-awakening, it's bound to attract all manner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:09.760
of investigators, scientists, tourists, and media.&nbsp;
Podcast won't be the only person investigating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:13.840
its mysteries anymore, and that could both&nbsp;
lead to good and bad things for the town.&nbsp;

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:14.640
"The entire Eastern seaboard is alive with talk&nbsp;
of incidents of paranormal activity. Alleged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:18.560
ghost sightings and related supernatural&nbsp;
occurrences have been reported across the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:20.160
entire tri-state area."

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:24.480
In the original "Ghostbusters," the team faced&nbsp;
Gozer as the ancient god took the form of a giant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:29.200
representation of the Stay-Puft Marshmallow Man.&nbsp;
After crossing the streams of their proton packs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:33.440
the Ghostbusters were able to defeat Gozer's&nbsp;
destroyer form and thus banish the god back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:37.920
to its own dimension, seemingly for good.
Of course, we now know that Gozer was just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:40.480
biding their time until they&nbsp;
could re-enter our dimension,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:45.200
but thankfully Egon Spengler had developed a plan.&nbsp;
Instead of just banishing the creature yet again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:49.440
he built an elaborate, high-powered trap on his&nbsp;
homestead in Oklahoma, waiting for the moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.520
that he could lure Gozer in and spring it. It&nbsp;
didn't work for Egon, but his granddaughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.080
her family and friends, and the surviving original&nbsp;
Ghostbusters were able to capture the creature.&nbsp;

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:02.560
The question is: With Gozer now&nbsp;
contained in a trap, what happens next?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:04.640
There's a good chance Gozer will need to be busted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:06.960
at least one more time.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:10.880
Over the course of the film, the mystery at the&nbsp;
heart of "Ghostbusters: Afterlife" is slowly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:16.080
unearthed, often quite literally. Eventually,&nbsp;
Phoebe, Trevor, Podcast, and Lucky discover a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:21.200
tomb/temple complex beneath the mountain built&nbsp;
in tribute to Gozer, the Sumerian god who first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:25.520
appeared in the original "Ghostbusters" film.
The tomb is full of interesting details,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:30.640
but Phoebe picks up one in particular that stands&nbsp;
out with regard to the franchise's future: A stone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:35.280
relief that features carved dates of various&nbsp;
years in which major catastrophes occurred.&nbsp;

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:39.360
What's especially interesting about these carvings&nbsp;
is that there appears to be another, partially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:45.200
obscured date carved into the rock sometime after&nbsp;
2021. It's difficult to make out exactly when it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:50.000
is, but Gozer's closest followers probably have&nbsp;
some idea, and the presence of the temple in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.120
Oklahoma suggests there could be others out there.
So, what future catastrophe awaits this next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.480
generation of Ghostbusters? Time will tell.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:03.360
"Ghostbusters: Afterlife" is a movie packed with&nbsp;
cameo appearances. Though she was confirmed to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:07.360
part of the film months before its release,&nbsp;
one former "Ghostbusters" star waited until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:12.240
the very end to show up: Dana Barrett, who&nbsp;
developed a romance with Dr. Peter Venkman in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:16.960
the first film and rekindled it in the second.
Dana finally appears in a mid-credits scene in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:21.440
the film that echoes our first meeting with&nbsp;
Venkman back in 1984, as she runs his old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:26.160
shock treatment ESP test on him. There's clear&nbsp;
flirtation happening between the two of them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:30.560
and Venkman even throws out the phrase "true&nbsp;
love" at one point. It's such a brief scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:34.640
that we don't get too many clues, but it's clear&nbsp;
that the filmmakers at least want us to think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:39.200
about what might be happening. Perhaps an eventual&nbsp;
"Afterlife" sequel could clear up just how well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.160
Peter and Dana are getting along these days.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:45.600
In one crucial scene in "Ghostbusters:&nbsp;
Afterlife," Phoebe calls the old number in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:50.800
a vintage Ghostbusters commercial and is connected&nbsp;
to Ray Stantz's occult bookshop in New York City.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:54.640
After a little nudging, she's able to get Ray&nbsp;
to tell her a little of the backstory behind the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:59.840
breakup of the Ghostbusters. According to Ray, it&nbsp;
had its roots in two things: Egon's obsession with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:05.040
the re-emergence of Gozer, and an almost complete&nbsp;
lack of new calls for supernatural assistance.&nbsp;

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:09.760
"There hasn't been a ghost sighting in 30 years."
Gozer's return obviously shook at least a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:13.520
ghosts loose, and at the very end of&nbsp;
the film we see ECTO-1 back in action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:18.240
but how many ghosts are there to really&nbsp;
bust? Gozer is, after all, in captivity now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:21.680
and the portal that awakened the god&nbsp;
of destruction seems to be dormant.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:25.120
Has something else shaken loose that will&nbsp;
guarantee continued work for the team,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:29.440
or are they just going to do what they can with&nbsp;
what they have for as long as possible? Obviously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:32.560
a sequel would help to clear this up quite a bit.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:36.640
In the post-credits scene of "Ghostbusters:&nbsp;
Afterlife," Winston Zeddemore and Janine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:40.880
Melnitz meet in New York City to discuss the&nbsp;
future of the Ghostbusters team. Winston's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:45.360
success in the world of finance means that he&nbsp;
has considerable resources at his disposal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:49.840
enough to buy back the firehouse, restore&nbsp;
ECTO-1, and get the team up and running again.&nbsp;

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:54.560
The question remaining is what exactly that team&nbsp;
will look like once Winston and Janine are all set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:58.400
up again. Will the Spengler family move back&nbsp;
to New York and be a part of the next era of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:03.120
the company, with Janine and Winston running the&nbsp;
show behind the scenes? It seems likely that if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.520
Winston and Janine are back in the game, Ray would&nbsp;
have a hard time not lurking around the firehouse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:12.320
himself, training new recruits. And Venkman?&nbsp;
Well, he might not care for busting anymore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:16.240
but even if he doesn't, he could be persuaded&nbsp;
to handle the marketing side of things.&nbsp;

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:20.080
It's easy to imagine that crew coming together&nbsp;
with the Spenglers to launch the next phase&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:24.880
of Ghostbusters Inc., and perhaps even do&nbsp;
what previous sequel ideas had in mind and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:28.960
franchise the whole thing, with locations&nbsp;
in every major city. Whatever the case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:33.600
the old firehouse is about to power up again, and&nbsp;
that trap grid in the basement might have a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:36.240
old terrors still lurking in it.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:38.160
Though Phoebe is the star of "Ghostbusters:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:41.120
Afterlife," you could make the case&nbsp;
that the most important character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:45.600
in the overall story is actually her&nbsp;
deceased grandfather, Dr. Egon Spengler.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:50.080
By the time of "Afterlife," Egon is a ghost,&nbsp;
lurking in his house in Oklahoma and biding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:54.720
his time until his genius granddaughter puts all&nbsp;
the pieces of his plant to defeat Gozer together.&nbsp;

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:58.880
While that happens, we learn that somewhere along&nbsp;
the way, he decided he had to make a massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:03.520
sacrifice in his quest to keep the world safe from&nbsp;
a dark god. When he couldn't convince his fellow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:08.400
Ghostbusters that Gozer was about to resurge, Egon&nbsp;
instead cut himself off from everyone with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:13.360
exception of Janine, moved to Oklahoma to be near&nbsp;
the old Gozer site, and abandoned both his family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:16.640
and his friends for their own protection.
"Do you have any hobbies?"

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:23.520
"I collect spores, molds, and fungus."
It's a move that speaks to his obsessive nature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:28.240
but also to his ability to think in terms of&nbsp;
the greater good. Egon's choices could easily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:32.400
be dismissed as part of his character as the&nbsp;
coldest Ghostbuster, but it took an enormous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:36.960
level of love and care for the people in his life&nbsp;
to do what he did. It was a sacrifice that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:41.440
film only scratched the surface of, but in the&nbsp;
end, it proved that Egon Spengler may have had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:46.400
the biggest heart of all of the Ghostbusters.
